spec
goal: route customer email deterministically without mutating the message

scope:
  edit: solution.py
  contract: route_email(message) -> {queue,priority,normalized_sender,normalized_recipients}

rules:
  R1: normalized sender/recipients = strip then lowercase; preserve recipient order and duplicates
  R2: content tokens = ASCII `[a-z0-9]+` matches from lowercase subject and body
  R3: sender domain after last `@` exactly spam.test or malware.test -> queue=spam, overriding all other routing
  R4: otherwise exact recipient local part billing/support/sales selects queue; precedence billing > support > sales
  R5: without R4, content token in invoice/payment/refund/charge -> billing
  R6: otherwise help/issue/error/bug -> support; otherwise quote/demo/pricing -> sales; otherwise general
  R7: recipient routing overrides content routing
  R8: spam -> priority=low; otherwise urgent/asap/outage content token -> high; otherwise normal
  R9: empty subject/body/recipients are valid; output has exactly four contract fields; preserve message and recipient list

acceptance:
  A1: R1,R9 preserve normalized recipient order, duplicates, and inputs
  A2: R2-R8 implement exact routing and precedence
  A3: empty content defaults to general/normal when unmatched
  A4: output is JSON-serializable and contains only contract fields
